6. Anisble Playbook
==================
Playbook = YAML file containing automation instructions.
Example:
- name:Configure web server
  hosts:web
  become:yes
  tasks:
  - name:Install nginx
    apt:
    name:nginx
    state:present
  - name:Start nginx
    service:
    name:nginx
    state:started
RUN: ansible-playbook -i inventory web.yaml

Playbook structure:
====================
Playbook
play --> Which servers ( hosts:web)
Tasks  --> What should happen? (- name:Install nginx)
Modules  --> Which ansible functionality? (apt)

***** Important Ansible Terms******
Controller ( Machine where Ansible runs)
Managed Node ( Server managed by ansible )
Inventory ( List/groups of target servers)
Module ( pre-built unit used to perform a task )
play ( collection of tasks for selected hosts)
playbook ( one or more plays written in YAML)

